# Cerebrum

> OpenWolf's learning memory. Updated automatically as the AI learns from interactions.
> Do not edit manually unless correcting an error.
> Last updated: 2026-04-03

## User Preferences

<!-- How the user likes things done. Code style, tools, patterns, communication. -->
- [2026-06-14] When fixing pre-delivery issues, the user prefers doing the frontend-only/safe items first and deferring backend-coupled money paths (payment payload changes) until the backend can change in lockstep. Document required backend changes in `API_CHANGES_AND_FIXES.md` rather than risking a broken checkout.

## Key Learnings

- **Project:** kv-silver-zone
- **Description:** Premium Silver selling eCommerce Platform
- Form validation uses zod schemas in `src/lib/validation.ts` + a `validateForm(schema, data)` helper returning `{ success, errors }` (flat field->message map). Forms keep raw `useState`, validate on submit, render inline `text-destructive` errors with `aria-invalid`. Indian phone rule: `^[6-9]\d{9}$` (tolerant of +91/spaces); PIN `^\d{6}$`.
- Protected routes are wrapped with `src/components/RequireAuth.tsx` in `App.tsx` (redirects to `/login` with `state.from`; Login returns the user there). `ErrorBoundary.tsx` wraps the route tree for render-error fallback.
- ProductDetail price breakdown prefers the server-computed `product.pricing` (`metalValue`, `makingCharge`, `ratePerGram`, `basis`) + `weightInGrams`; falls back to live `silverRateService.getTodayRate()` × weight, then a 75/25 split — display only; server stays authoritative for the charge.
- Auth is cookie-based (httpOnly) on the **web** build: `api.ts` sends `credentials: 'include'`, sets NO `Authorization` header. Logout must call `POST /auth/logout` (JS can't clear an httpOnly cookie). Only the user object is cached in `localStorage` (`kv-silver-user`). **Mobile (Capacitor) build is different:** `isMobileApp()` (in `src/lib/platform.ts`) is true, so `api.ts` attaches `Authorization: Bearer <token>` from `localStorage['kv-silver-token']`; `AuthContext` now persists the login/signup response `token` (previously ignored) and clears it on logout/401. Backend MUST accept Bearer on protected routes for the mobile app to work.
- GST percent is read from `GET /pricing-config` via `src/services/pricingConfig.ts` (default 3%) — used in `CartContext`, `Payment`, `ProductDetail`. Do NOT hardcode GST (Payment previously used 5% while Cart used 3%).
- Gift vouchers come from `GET /gift-vouchers` (`src/services/giftVoucher.ts`). Voucher cart items must carry `isGiftVoucher: true` + `giftVoucherId`; these flow into create-order and verify line items so the server prices them.
- Checkout: `POST /payments/create-order` takes `{ items:[{product,quantity,isGiftVoucher?,giftVoucherId?}], couponCode?, pincode? }` (NO client amount) and returns the authoritative `{ id, amount, currency, breakdown? }`. Never send a client-computed total as authoritative.
- SEO uses `react-helmet-async`: `<HelmetProvider>` wraps the tree in `App.tsx`; per-page `<Seo title description image? type? noindex?>` from `src/components/Seo.tsx`. IMPORTANT: any test that renders a page using `<Seo>` must wrap render in `<HelmetProvider>` or Helmet throws "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'add')".
- Per-endpoint frontend↔API contracts live in `docs/api/` (one md per endpoint) — update them when a request/response shape changes.
- Saved checkout address: `Payment.tsx` persists/loads the shipping address in `localStorage` under `kv-silver-address` (separate from `kv-silver-user`/`kv-silver-cart`).
- **`openapi.json` at repo root is the source of truth for API shapes** — consult it before assuming response fields. Several list/config endpoints wrap payloads in `{ status, data }` (e.g. `/gift-vouchers`, `/pricing-config`, `/products/categories`) while `/products`, `/products/{id}`, `/products/featured` return bare. GiftVoucher uses `label`+`amount`+`sortOrder`; `ProductPricing.basis` is enum `'live'|'static'`.
- Analytics/monitoring in `src/lib/analytics.ts` — `@sentry/react` + GA4, gated on `VITE_SENTRY_DSN`/`VITE_GA4_ID`, no-op when blank. `initMonitoring()` in `main.tsx`; SPA page views via `trackPageview` in `AppContent` on route change.
- Invoice download: `react-to-print` v3 `useReactToPrint({ contentRef })` in `OrderTracking.tsx`, printing the off-screen `InvoiceView` (forwardRef).
- E2E: Playwright config at root, tests in `e2e/` (vitest `include` is `src/**` so no collision). `npm run test:e2e`; first run needs `npx playwright install chromium`.
- Address book: `src/services/address.ts` (`/users/me/addresses` CRUD, bare array; `Address` has `label`/`isDefault`; `AddressInput` omits `id`). `Payment.tsx` shows a saved-address picker for authed users, prefills the default, and POSTs a new address on order success (dedup by address+pincode+phone); guests still use `localStorage` `kv-silver-address`. Order confirmation email is automatic server-side; `orderService.resendConfirmation(id)` (`POST /orders/{id}/resend-confirmation`) powers the "Resend email" button on `OrderConfirmation.tsx`.
- Password changes use `PUT /users/:userId/password` with body `{ newPassword }`, and UI should map status codes 400/403/404 to user-facing validation messages.
- Admin user-management actions can be role-gated inside `src/pages/Admin.tsx` using `role === 'admin'`, while staff may still access other admin tabs.
- Storefront theme should be fetched from public `GET /store-config` on app startup, with localStorage only as fallback.
- Admin theme management should read from `GET /admin/store-config` and update through `/admin/store-config` (PUT with POST fallback for compatibility).
- **Push notifications (mobile):** Capacitor `@capacitor/push-notifications` (FCM on Android). `src/components/PushNotifications.tsx` (mounted in `App.tsx` inside auth+router providers, renders null) requests permission, registers, shows foreground notifications as a toast, and deep-links on tap via `data.route`. Gated to `isMobileApp()` + authenticated; plugin loaded via dynamic import so it stays out of the web bundle. `src/services/push.ts` → `POST/DELETE /users/me/push-tokens` (`{ token, platform }`) — NOT yet implemented backend-side (see `docs/push-notifications.md` + API_CHANGES_AND_FIXES.md). Gradle auto-applies google-services only when `android/app/google-services.json` exists, so build stays green without Firebase; push silently no-ops until that file + a Firebase project are added. No auto-unregister on logout (DELETE would be unauthenticated after token clear).
- **Mobile app (Capacitor/Android):** customer-only app shares the web codebase. `npm run build:mobile` (= `cross-env VITE_APP_TARGET=mobile vite build`) builds it; `IS_MOBILE_BUILD` (in `src/lib/platform.ts`) gates the `/admin` route in `App.tsx` and the Admin nav link in `Navbar.tsx`. The Admin lazy import is in a dead `IS_MOBILE_BUILD ? null : lazy(...)` branch so Rollup drops the Admin chunk from the mobile bundle entirely (verified: no `Admin-*.js` emitted). Native project in `android/`; sync with `npm run mobile:sync`, open with `mobile:open`, run with `mobile:run`. `capacitor.config.ts` → appId `com.kvsilverzone.app`, webDir `dist`. VITE_API_URL must point to a device-reachable server (emulator: `10.0.2.2`), not localhost.

- **Product size/weight variants:** `Product.variants?: ProductVariant[]` (`{ label, weight, height?, breadth? }`, all strings) in `src/context/CartContext.tsx`. Free-text `label` (S–XXL style); `weight` will drive the total calc (next phase, not yet wired to cart/price); `height`/`breadth` are display-only. Normalized in `src/services/product.ts` (`normalizeVariants` trims + drops rows with no label/weight). Admin create+edit forms use a shared `VariantsEditor` component in `Admin.tsx` (rows stripped via `cleanVariants` before POST/PUT). `ProductDetail.tsx` shows a size selector that swaps the displayed weight/height/breadth. `ProductCard.tsx` lists available weights (`20g / 30g / 40g`). Backend must persist/echo `variants` on `/products`, `/products/:id`, `/admin/products` — contract in `docs/api/products-variants.md`.

- **Product pricing config (fixed price + making charge + wastage):** `Product.isFixedPrice?: boolean`, `makingCharge?: ProductCharge`, `wastage?: ProductCharge` where `ProductCharge = { type: 'percentage'|'amount', value: number }` (`ChargeType` in `CartContext.tsx`). Normalized in `product.ts` (`normalizeCharge` — drops non-finite values, defaults unknown type to `percentage`). Admin forms (`Admin.tsx`) have a Fixed-Price `Switch` + two `ChargeInput` rows (type Select + numeric value) with inline validation via `validateCharge` (empty allowed; value ≥ 0; percentage ≤ 100); submit disabled while invalid. Fixed-price ON hides+omits making/wastage. `ProductDetail.tsx` hides the estimated price-breakdown block when `isFixedPrice`. making/wastage feed the dynamic price calc — NOT yet wired to cart total (next phase). Backend contract: `docs/api/products-pricing-config.md`. Convention: write ONE new md per API change in `docs/api/` (user preference, 2026-06-15).

- **Zone-based delivery charges:** `src/services/deliveryConfig.ts` — `DeliveryConfig { chennai, otherDistrict, otherState }` (₹, defaults 150/200/250), `resolveDeliveryZone({city,state})` (Chennai=home city → chennai; Tamil Nadu → otherDistrict; else otherState, case-insensitive), `getDeliveryCharge(config, address)`. Public `GET /delivery-config`; admin `GET`/`PUT /admin/delivery-config`. Admin UI is in `Admin.tsx` Shipping tab → "Delivery Charges" card (3 editable amounts + Save, validated ≥0). NOTE: an older in-memory "Delivery Fee Matrix" (pincode→rate, `pincodeRates` useState, NOT persisted/no API) still lives in the same tab — it's a mock; the zone card is the real one. Checkout money-path wiring (add zone charge to create-order `amount`/`breakdown` + replace "Shipping: Free" in `Payment.tsx`) is DEFERRED — see `docs/api/delivery-config.md` + API_CHANGES_AND_FIXES.md. Contract: `docs/api/delivery-config.md`.

- **Shop price filter:** `src/pages/Shop.tsx` has a two-handle price range **slider** (`PriceRangeSlider`, built on `@radix-ui/react-slider` directly because the shared `ui/slider.tsx` renders only one thumb and per CLAUDE.md ui primitives must not be hand-edited) plus the original preset radio buckets — they're mutually exclusive (`priceSlider` state overrides `selectedPriceRange`; each clears the other). Slider range is FIXED ₹100–₹5,000 (`PRICE_MIN`/`PRICE_MAX`/`PRICE_STEP=100` consts; was product-derived before 2026-06-16). Handles at the extremes ⇒ no cap on that end (`minPrice` undefined at floor, `maxPrice` undefined at ceiling), label shows "₹5,000+". `productService.getProducts` already accepts `minPrice`/`maxPrice` (frontend-only, no API change).
- **Test infra:** `src/test/setup.ts` stubs `window.matchMedia` AND now `ResizeObserver` (jsdom lacks it; Radix Slider needs it). Any new test rendering a Radix component that measures size relies on this stub — see [[bug-030]].

- **Docs layout (2026-06-16):** all project markdown was flattened into `docs/` and numbered oldest→newest (`01-...` … `21-...`); `docs/README.md` is the master index (chronological list + contract→client-file map). `plans/` and `docs/api/` folders were removed. Excluded/left in place: `README.md` (root), `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/`, `.wolf/`. NOTE: older cerebrum entries and in-code comments may still reference pre-move paths like `docs/api/<name>.md` or root `API_CHANGES_AND_FIXES.md` — these now live under `docs/NN-*.md` (e.g. delivery-config → `docs/21-delivery-config.md`, products-variants → `docs/19-products-variants.md`, products-pricing-config → `docs/20-products-pricing-config.md`, api-changes-and-fixes → `docs/09-api-changes-and-fixes.md`). Use `docs/README.md` to resolve.

- **Multiple product images:** `Product.images?: string[]` (normalized srcs, ordered; `image` = primary = images[0]) in `CartContext.tsx`. `product.ts` `extractImages()` sorts API `images[{imageBase64,sortOrder}]` and normalizes, falling back to the flat `image`. Admin (`Admin.tsx`) uses a self-contained `ImagesUploader` (multi-file, thumbnail grid, remove + "make primary" reorder) in both forms; payload sends `image` (primary) + `images: string[]`. Sliding gallery via reusable `src/components/ProductImageCarousel.tsx` (embla `ui/carousel`) on `ProductCard.tsx` (hover arrows + dots) and `ProductDetail.tsx` (`alwaysShowControls`); falls back to plain `<img>` for a single image. IMPORTANT pattern: carousel lives inside ProductCard's `<Link>` — control buttons use `onClickCapture` with `e.preventDefault()+stopPropagation()` to avoid navigating (don't pass `onClick`, it would override embla's scroll handler). Write contract: `docs/22-products-multiple-images.md` (backend write side TBD).

- **Shop slider debounce + infinite scroll:** Price slider is debounced (`PRICE_DEBOUNCE_MS`, currently 700ms; module-level const) — `priceSlider` (live, drives `sliderValue` display) → `appliedPriceSlider` (debounced, drives query key + min/max); clearing to null (presets) applies immediately. Product list uses `useInfiniteQuery` (`PAGE_SIZE=12`, `initialPageParam:1`) with an `IntersectionObserver` sentinel (`rootMargin:400px`) for auto-load; results flattened + de-duped by id. `getNextPageParam` stops on empty/partial page, on a page LARGER than limit (unpaginated backend returned all), or when a full page repeats already-seen ids — so it degrades gracefully (shows all once, no dup fetches) until backend adds `page`/`limit`. `ProductFilters` gained `page?`/`limit?`. Contract: `docs/23-products-pagination.md`. Backend `/products` pagination NOT yet implemented.
- **Test infra:** `src/test/setup.ts` now also stubs `IntersectionObserver` (jsdom lacks it; infinite-scroll sentinel uses it) — alongside `matchMedia` + `ResizeObserver`. See [[bug-030]].

## Do-Not-Repeat

<!-- Mistakes made and corrected. Each entry prevents the same mistake recurring. -->
<!-- Format: [YYYY-MM-DD] Description of what went wrong and what to do instead. -->
- [2026-06-14] A `validateForm` helper typed as a discriminated union `{success:true;data} | {success:false;errors}` failed TS narrowing under `if (!result.success)` at call sites (TS2339 on `.errors`). Fixed by returning a single shape `{ success: boolean; errors: Record<string,string> }` (errors empty when valid). Forms read `formData` directly, so the parsed `data` wasn't needed.
- [2026-06-14] Bug-029: `Shop.tsx handleSearchChange` called `setSelectedPriceRanges([])` (plural) — setter is `setSelectedPriceRange('')` (singular string). Typing in search threw ReferenceError. Verify setter names match useState declarations.
- [2026-06-14] Adding `<Seo>` (react-helmet-async) to a page broke `Shop.test.tsx` with "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'add')" because the test render had no `<HelmetProvider>`. Fix: wrap page-render test helpers in `<HelmetProvider>`. Applies to any future test rendering a page that uses `<Seo>`.

## Decision Log

<!-- Significant technical decisions with rationale. Why X was chosen over Y. -->
- [2026-04-05] Implemented a dedicated `ChangePassword` page for normal users and a separate admin-only modal action in the customers table, both hitting the same endpoint for consistent backend behavior.
- [2026-04-05] Switched theme persistence to backend store-config endpoints for both public app initialization and admin save flow.
- [2026-06-14] Chose Capacitor (over React Native rewrite or PWA-only) to ship a customer-only Android app, because admin is isolated to one route so the existing React SPA could be reused near-100%. Kept it in the same repo behind a `VITE_APP_TARGET=mobile` build flag (vs a separate mobile config or repo fork) for one source of truth. Mobile auth uses Bearer tokens instead of the httpOnly cookie because the Capacitor WebView origin can't share the web cookie cross-origin.
